# Site-wide security baseline (2026-08-14 launch-readiness round). Additive
# header names only — these never collide with the Cache-Control rules below.
# HSTS: 180 days after a 30-day soak (2026-08-14 -> 2026-09-10). No
# includeSubDomains, no preload. (It used to be excluded because api.degener.us
# was a separate host; that host is gone and the session service is same-origin
# now, but adding includeSubDomains is still its own soak and its own decision.)
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# CSP ENFORCING since 2026-08-15, after a full report-only pass (cold load,
# every panel, replay/reveal overlays, settings, referrals, and the live
# WalletConnect QR modal — 878-request esm.sh SDK graph + relay + web3modal)
# surfaced exactly three missing origins, all added below.
# Origins: publicnode/base.org = chain RPC (MAINNET CUTOVER: add the mainnet
# RPC hosts here — prepare-chain-deployment.mjs --activate appends them); esm.sh =
# lazy WalletConnect SDK; walletconnect/web3modal = WC relay, config, verify
# iframe, wallet icons, RPC fallback; discord CDN = avatars; blob: = the badge bundle store;
# cloudflareinsights = the zone's auto-injected Web Analytics beacon (script)
# and its /cdn-cgi/rum POST target (connect).
# REMOVED 2026-09-22: degenerus-db.fly.dev (the indexer API) and api.degener.us
# (the session server). Both hosts were destroyed; the app reads chain state
# over RPC and the session service is same-origin ('self') at /session/*. A CSP
# entry for a dead host grants nothing and only makes the policy read as if the
# dependency were still live. Google Fonts origins were
# dropped 2026-08-15 when Inter moved to self-hosted /shared/fonts/.
# script-src: the 'unsafe-inline' token below is a PLACEHOLDER. db/publish-app.sh
# runs db/csp-inline-hashes.mjs on the publication overlay, which replaces it
# with the sha256 hash of every inline <script> in the published HTML under
# /app/ (and the /beta/ entry copy), so the live policy admits only authored
# inline scripts. Inline event handler attributes and javascript: URLs have no
# hash and FAIL the publish; index.html flips its deferred stylesheets from a
# hashed head listener for that reason. 'report-sample' puts the first 40
# characters of a refused inline script into the violation event that
# index.html beacons to telemetry. The dev server applies no CSP, so this
# file is inert locally; db/post-publish-smoke.mjs checks the LIVE header
# carries hashes and no 'unsafe-inline'. Cloudflare JavaScript Detections
# injects an inline challenge script before </body> that the hashed policy
# refuses (one CSP violation per load): turn that feature off in the
# Cloudflare dashboard, or accept the console line.
